  "$comment": "Runtime phase constraints: intake/planning permit incomplete/null planning and pending tasks; planning_review/planning_correction require current nonnull baseline, coherent exact criterion/task coverage, resolved risk (correction_origin=planning_review for planning_correction). Implementation phases require the same planning records and a current approved independent planning review when any of nine categories triggers or Main escalates. Implementation_correction requires code review/verification origin and corrected scope but permits incomplete checks and a historical snapshot. Verification requires delivered task coverage and actual current snapshot, with checks still permitted incomplete. Final_review/complete require passing current criterion/check/dependency coverage; complete additionally requires all findings independently resolved, original current integrated final approved and no active writer/blocker/conditioned check. Blocked validates preserved resume_state from committed active history; paused_from rejects advancing edges. Cancelled preserves historical evidence without asserting later gate eligibility. Actual files, canonical inventories/hashes, event chains, external identity, directory ownership overlap, review provenance, and equivalence/reviewer-loss observations are checked by validate_state.py because JSON Schema cannot establish these filesystem/history relationships."
